I've written the Day 252 assessment and committed it as f67c7c91. Commit e571c191 bumped yoagent to 0.27.3. That release adds one setting to yoagent's model config, accepts_sampling_params, which says whether a model accepts a temperature. @yuanhao's note closing #1146 (13:01Z) spells out what yoyo should do next. I didn't re-run the test suite; the harness had already checked it was green at the start of the session.

What I checked:
• Single prompt: yoyo -p answered PONG on claude-opus-5-5 and exited 0.
• #1127 (shell commands showing chat-window syntax): all six remaining commands still print /verb usage in the shell instead of yoyo verb: docs, lint, risk, skill, map and memories.
• #1150 (extra words after `-p` silently dropped): I didn't run this one. Like the ticket, my read of it comes from the code only.

Recommended order for the planner:
1. Use yoagent's new temperature setting. @yuanhao wrote: "Replace #1145's own version check with config.accepts_sampling_params. Keep the stderr note when the user set a temperature and the flag is false." yoyo's own copy of the check (in src/temperature_support.rs) only knows the anthropic and bedrock providers. So an OpenRouter user who sets --temperature on a newer Claude model has the value dropped by yoagent and gets no note saying so. #1145 and #1146 are both closed, so this task needs Part of #1122 or a new issue to track it.
2. #1150: yoyo -p hi extra sends only hi, and since this morning's #1114 fix it also swallows claude-zzz in yoyo --system --model claude-zzz -p hi. Run it against the built binary first, then decide whether to refuse or warn. The precedent is #1109, where an unknown flag exits 2 and nothing is sent.
3. #1127: the six commands above. Each is a small change using the existing command_form helper.
4. #1114: two helpers still mistake a flag's value for another flag: collect_repeatable_flag and resolve_numeric_setting.
• Skip #1149, the question of whether -p should keep auto-approving every tool call. It's waiting on @yuanhao.

Size-limit hazards:
• src/help.rs can grow 10 more lines before cargo test fails, which reverts the whole task. Any edit there must update its entry in tests/module_size.rs in the same diff.
• src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs can grow 14 more lines and isn't listed in that file at all.
• src/cli.rs sits exactly at its recorded size.

Research: Claude Code 2.1.319 (Nov 6) has a few changes that match problems yoyo may share; I saved them to yopedia, but haven't tried any against yoyo:
• A third permission option: permissions.denyInsteadOfPrompting refuses a tool call instead of asking, and the turn carries on. That's useful information for @yuanhao on #1149.
• Exit code after refusals: they fixed claude -p exiting 0 when its actions were refused.
• Slash commands after leading spaces: they fixed commands typed after a leading space being sent as plain text.

I didn't look at Cursor, Codex or Aider this time.
